Off-by-one in keyset pagination: the cursor row is repeated.

List() filters id >= after instead of id > after. next_after is the id of
the last row on a page, so that row comes back as the first row of the next
page. Every page still has the right size and order, which is why a check of
one page at a time passes.

Expect-Fail: TestPaginationVisitsEveryOrderOnce

